SIM-09: start the hydraulic reporting clock on the Rstart grid

inithyd() set the first reporting time Rtime to Rstep, ignoring Rstart,
so the hydraulic time steps only landed on multiples of Rstep. With a
report start that is not a multiple of the report step, no solution was
computed at the reporting times, and the water quality pass stored the
next solution under each label. Set Rtime to the first time after 0 on
the grid Rstart + k*Rstep. When Rstart is a multiple of Rstep (or 0),
this is Rstep as before, so those runs are unchanged.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply SIM-09_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/hydraul.c b/src/hydraul.c
index fa96868..ac79800 100755
--- a/src/hydraul.c
+++ b/src/hydraul.c
@@ -182,7 +182,10 @@ void inithyd(Project *pr, int initflag)
     hyd->Haltflag = 0;
     time->Htime = 0;
     time->Hydstep = 0;
-    time->Rtime = time->Rstep;
+
+    // First reporting time after 0 on the grid Rstart + k*Rstep
+    time->Rtime = time->Rstart % time->Rstep;
+    if (time->Rtime == 0) time->Rtime = time->Rstep;
 }
 
 
